      'title': 'The Core Innovation: Understanding Self-Attention',
      'details': 'This critical transition section clarifies the crucial distinction between traditional attention and self-attention. Old (Encoder-Decoder) Attention involved the decoder looking at the encoder\'s output, while New (Self-Attention) means the input sequence looks at *itself*—all words in a sentence are related to each other simultaneously to create a richer understanding. Use a detailed analogy: to interpret the meaning of the word "it" in the sentence "The animal didn\'t cross the street because it was too tired," the model learns to assign high attention weights to "animal" and low weights to "street," figuring out relationships between all words. Briefly note that the mathematical dot product is scaled to maintain stable gradients during training, preventing the softmax function from becoming saturated.',
